@page
@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Developer Enablement"; }
<header class="page-header">
    <p class="page-kicker">
        <i class="bi bi-tools" aria-hidden="true"></i> Shared engineering foundations
    </p>
    <h1>
        Developer Enablement
    </h1>
    <p class="page-intro">
        Reusable applications, tooling, and guidance that support consistent product development.
    </p>
</header>
<div class="reading-layout">
    <nav class="section-nav" aria-label="On this page">
        <h2>
            On this page
        </h2>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <a href="#application-foundations">Application Foundations</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="#developer-toolbox">Developer Toolbox</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="#ai-guidance">Portable AI Engineering Guidance</a>
            </li>
            <li>
                <a href="#adoption">Architecture and Adoption</a>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </nav>
    <div class="reading-main">
        <section class="content-panel prose">
            <h2 id="application-foundations">
                Application Foundations
            </h2>
            <p>
                I created reusable C#/.NET and Node.js/React starter projects and have delivered full-stack production applications using these shared resources. The foundations bring together ASP.NET Core APIs, Next.js clients, shared .NET libraries, Aspire orchestration, automated validation, and delivery templates.
            </p>
            <p>
                A focused marketing website foundation adds feature-based boundaries, reusable UI components, localization, design tokens, and defensive API integration. These resources turn architecture and engineering practices into working starting points for product development.
            </p>
            <h2 id="developer-toolbox">
                Developer Toolbox
            </h2>
            <p>
                I developed shared local-development resources with Dev Containers, containerized database and service dependencies, and PowerShell/Bash setup and teardown tooling. Consumer-repository bootstrap scripts preserve existing files while adding shared setup support.
            </p>
            <p>
                The toolbox provides local services for databases, caching, storage, messaging, email capture, API mocking, and telemetry. Separating shared infrastructure from individual application repositories gives those responsibilities a clear owner.
            </p>
            <h2 id="ai-guidance">
                Portable AI Engineering Guidance
            </h2>
            <p>
                My developer tooling includes a curated library of engineering instructions, roles, prompts, and skills with synchronized adapters for GitHub Copilot, Codex, and Claude Code. Canonical guidance provides a shared foundation across tools while preserving the discovery conventions each tool uses.
            </p>
            <p>
                I combine that guidance with human review, testing, verification, and clear ownership of consequential decisions.
            </p>
            <h2 id="adoption">
                Architecture and Adoption
            </h2>
            <p>
                I provide technology reviews that support approval for adoption and implementation. My broader work includes standards, automation scaffolding, reusable QA templates, training, and practical guidance for engineering teams.
            </p>
            <p>
                <a asp-page="/Skills/Containers">Docker and Podman</a> · <a asp-page="/Skills/AI">AI engineering</a> · <a asp-page="/Experience/EmploymentAccomplishments" asp-fragment="developer-enablement">Developer toolbox accomplishments</a>
            </p>
        </section>
    </div>
    <aside class="reading-aside">
        <section class="content-panel">
            <h2>
                Skills and technologies
            </h2>
            <ul class="tag-list">
                <li>
